  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Friday)\nIssued at 1125 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nUpper ridge expands further eastward Sunday through Tuesday and a\nsteady rise in daytime highs are expected. Dewpoint trends may be\nslightly drier but confidence is low in exactly how much. Despite\nthe exact values, the overall pattern is supportive of continued \ndangerous heat through early week and further heat headlines are \nexpected. \n\nPotential for a weak frontal passage Monday night into Tuesday\nwith the upper ridge slightly weaker by mid to late week. The\nstalled frontal zone on periphery of the upper ridge may allow an\nincrease in shower and storm chances and slightly cooler\ntemperatures. There does remain a notable spread in ensemble\nguidance at this range so the magnitude and timing of any cool\ndown is uncertain.",
